# Project context documentation

After **major changes** to steam-monitor, update `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` in the same work session (same PR/commit when applicable).

## What counts as major

- New or removed modules under `app/`, `web/`, `scripts/`
- SQLite schema changes (`app/models.py`)
- New/changed environment variables (`app/config.py`, `.env.example`)
- Docker / compose / Dockerfile workflow changes
- Telegram alert flow, signal engine rules, or dashboard features
- Roadmap items completed or new known issues discovered

## What to update

Edit the relevant sections: architecture, folder structure, Docker, schema, Telegram logic, signals, dashboard, env vars, commands, roadmap, known issues, trading strategy.

Bump the **Last updated** date at the top of `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`.

## What to skip

- Typo fixes, small refactors, or comment-only changes that do not change behavior or structure.
